# War between your own factions (DESIGN.md §9.4): when a relation change puts two of a
# character's factions in conflict, a war opens for the game, a quest or the automatic rule
# to settle. Riverhold asks.
load content/sample
# Vex, a fence of the Guild, joins the Free Company: 12.31 away, within its 60.
join vex free_company
relate lantern_guild free_company -60
show character vex
# Vex keeps the Guild. Leaving the Company costs 10.00 there, and the Guild, now at -60
# with it, takes -0.06 of that the other way: +0.60.
resolve vex lantern_guild
assert resolve vex lantern_guild == error: vex has no open conflict involving lantern_guild
assert show character vex == vex — Vex — law -55.00, good -20.00 — Chaotic Neutral — member of lantern_guild (fence) since tick 0

# Peace before anyone settles it ends the war, and Vex keeps both.
load content/sample
join vex free_company
relate lantern_guild free_company -60
relate lantern_guild free_company -40
assert show character vex == vex — Vex — law -55.00, good -20.00 — Chaotic Neutral — member of free_company (sellsword) since tick 0, lantern_guild (fence) since tick 0
